# Compare Enum values by `.value`

When comparing Enum members, always compare `.value` on both sides. Do not rely on Enum identity or direct `==` between Enum instances.

Notebook autoreload can redefine the Enum class, so two members that look the same may fail `==` because they are different Python types.

## Preferred

```python
if estimation_mode.value == ReliabilityEstimationMode.POSITION_DEPENDENT.value:
    ...
```

## Avoid

```python
if estimation_mode == ReliabilityEstimationMode.POSITION_DEPENDENT:
    ...
```
